      "justification": "These 2,094 player-seasons, 55 percent of all defenders in the sample, are the central defenders, recovered from the statistics rather than read off the position label. Touches in the defensive third average 31.71 per 90 against 18.97 for the other defender cluster, touches in their own penalty area 7.75 against 3.34 and possession adjusted clearances 4.98 against 2.45, which places this centroid 0.68 standard deviations above the defender mean on defensive third touches and 0.62 standard deviations above it on clearances. They win 62.0 percent of their aerial duels against 49.7 percent, and they complete 90.0 percent of medium range passes against 80.4 percent and 67.5 percent of long passes against 51.4 percent, so their distribution is short, safe and lateral. The attacking side of the profile is close to absent: crosses per 90 of 0.24 against 2.39, touches in the attacking third 3.56 against 18.97 and shot creating actions 0.57 against 1.80. Representative members are \u00c7a\u011flar S\u00f6y\u00fcnc\u00fc, Lo\u00efc Perrin, Nicolas Nkoulou, Benjamin Pavard and Diego Llorente. The listed position does not encode this split, since most members of both defender clusters are listed simply as DF, which is the point: the clustering separates centre backs from wide defenders on measured behaviour where the label cannot. Membership is stable across time and competition: between 4 and 7 percent of defenders who play two consecutive seasons change cluster, the adjusted Rand index between consecutive seasons runs from 0.72 to 0.84, and refitting the same two cluster partition inside a single league recovers the pooled one with an adjusted Rand index from 0.89 to 0.97."
