      "justification": "These 1,699 player-seasons are the wide defenders, and the separation from their central counterparts is the sharpest contrast in the study. Crosses average 2.39 per 90 against 0.24 for the central cluster, which places this centroid 0.92 standard deviations above the defender mean, touches in the attacking third 18.97 against 3.56, progressive receptions 2.37 against 0.44 and carries into the final third 1.71 against 0.49. The creation follows: key passes per 90 of 0.93 against 0.19, passes into the penalty area 1.08 against 0.21 and shot creating actions 1.80 against 0.57. They attempt 1.62 take-ons per 90 against 0.41 and complete a smaller share of them, 56.7 percent against 71.7 percent, which is what attempting them in wide areas against a set defence costs. The defensive side is correspondingly lighter, with possession adjusted clearances 2.45 against 4.98 and 49.7 percent of aerial duels won against 62.0 percent. Representative members are Jos\u00e9 Luis Gay\u00e0, Sergio Reguil\u00f3n, Stefan Lainer, Timothy Castagne and K\u00e9vin Rodrigues, all full backs or wing backs. Membership is stable across time and competition: between 4 and 7 percent of defenders who play two consecutive seasons change cluster, the adjusted Rand index between consecutive seasons runs from 0.72 to 0.84, and refitting the same two cluster partition inside a single league recovers the pooled one with an adjusted Rand index from 0.89 to 0.97."
