      "justification": "These 1,939 player-seasons are the deep midfielders. Ball recoveries average 10.49 per 90 against 7.10 for the advanced cluster, possession adjusted tackles 2.34 against 1.57 and possession adjusted interceptions 1.31 against 0.82, and they win 49.6 percent of their aerial duels against 33.5 percent. Their touches sit behind the ball, 14.86 per 90 in the defensive third against 7.58 and 37.40 in the middle third against 26.22. The detail that matters is that they are not passive in possession: passes into the final third average 4.07 per 90 against 2.53 and progressive passes 4.00 against 3.48, both above the midfield mean, so they advance the ball by playing it forward rather than by carrying it or receiving it high up the pitch. What separates them is where the move ends for them, since touches in the opposition penalty area average 1.12 per 90 against 3.47, progressive receptions 2.16 against 6.46 and shots 0.93 against 1.92. Representative members are Jo\u00e3o Moutinho, Douglas Luiz, Sandro Tonali, Luka Milivojevi\u0107 and Oriol Romeu. Membership is stable across time and competition: between 9 and 10 percent of midfielders who play two consecutive seasons change cluster, the adjusted Rand index between consecutive seasons runs from 0.63 to 0.67, and refitting the same two cluster partition inside a single league recovers the pooled one with an adjusted Rand index from 0.72 to 0.97."
