      "justification": "These 1,827 player-seasons are the advanced and wide attacking midfielders, and the listed position half agrees, since the most common single listed value inside the cluster is the dual designation MF,FW. Progressive receptions average 6.46 per 90 against 2.16 for the deep cluster, which is 0.81 standard deviations above the midfield mean, touches in the opposition penalty area 3.47 against 1.12, touches in the attacking third 24.05 against 12.74 and progressive carries 6.02 against 3.83. Output follows from that position: shots per 90 of 1.92 against 0.93, non-penalty expected goals 0.18 against 0.07, key passes 1.52 against 0.81 and crosses 1.97 against 0.62. They defend much less, with ball recoveries per 90 of 7.10 against 10.49 and possession adjusted tackles 1.57 against 2.34, and they complete a smaller share of their passing at every distance, 84.1 percent short against 87.7 percent and 78.5 percent at medium range against 86.6 percent, which is what passing into congested areas costs. Representative members are Brais M\u00e9ndez, Andreas Pereira, Nathan Redmond, Hamed Junior Traor\u00e8 and Gio Reyna. Membership is stable across time and competition: between 9 and 10 percent of midfielders who play two consecutive seasons change cluster, the adjusted Rand index between consecutive seasons runs from 0.63 to 0.67, and refitting the same two cluster partition inside a single league recovers the pooled one with an adjusted Rand index from 0.72 to 0.97."
