      "justification": "These 1,241 player-seasons are 73 percent of all forwards and are defined by what they do not do rather than by any positive extreme. Their shooting sits at the forward average, with non-penalty expected goals of 0.34 per 90 against 0.30 for the other forward cluster and non-penalty goals of 0.32 against 0.31, and their box presence is close to average as well, with touches in the opposition penalty area of 4.92 against 5.39. Everything that happens before the shot sits well below average. Progressive carries average 2.56 per 90 against 7.04, progressive passes 1.40 against 3.34, passes into the penalty area 0.55 against 1.55, shot creating actions 2.11 against 3.69 and touches in the middle third 16.50 against 23.38. They also complete less of their short passing, 77.3 percent against 84.3 percent. Representative members are Ollie Watkins, Jo\u00e3o Pedro, Enes \u00dcnal, Habib Diallo and Luis Javier Su\u00e1rez. This is the centre forward who is fed rather than the one who builds, and the honest reading of the cluster is low involvement outside the box rather than a distinct finishing skill, because none of the finishing statistics separate the two forward clusters. Membership is stable across time and competition: between 8 and 11 percent of forwards who play two consecutive seasons change cluster, the adjusted Rand index between consecutive seasons runs from 0.58 to 0.67, and refitting the same two cluster partition inside a single league recovers the pooled one with an adjusted Rand index from 0.66 to 0.99."
